<VI _name="lvbd_graft_rewire.vi" description="Second half of lvai_graft_diagram. After lvbd_graft_paste, every supplied control X has a pasted duplicate that carries the wires. For each pair named in Originals and Duplicates this helper reads the duplicate terminal's wire ends, moves the ORIGINAL terminal onto the duplicate terminal's diagram and position, optionally copies the duplicate's description, deletes the duplicate, and connects the original to the recorded ends. It then removes the loose wire ends the deletes leave behind and saves the VI in place.\0A\0AWHY BD.Remove Bad Wires IS NOT OPTIONAL\3A deleting a control removes its terminal but leaves the wire's loose end at every former sink. Measured 2026-09-30\3A without it the grafted VI is eBad, with it executable.\0A\0AWHY THE TERMINAL IS MOVED TWICE\3A Position reads in pane coordinates while Move takes a position relative to the OWNER diagram, so a terminal moved into a loop landed offset by the loop's diagram origin, measured at about 425 by 22 px. The first Move reveals the offset, the second applies target + target - landed, which is correct whichever convention Move really uses.\0A\0ACONTROLS ARE FOUND BY LABEL, and their references are read once before the loop, so a deletion cannot shift a later lookup. A control terminal is a SOURCE, so its former SINKS are reconnected; an indicator terminal is a SINK, so its former SOURCE is. Auto Route? is wired TRUE, because at its FALSE default LabVIEW registers the wire and draws nothing.\0A\0AOpened in the IDE application instance through Application\3AProject\3AActive Project.">
